    "posts": [
      {
        "id": 16892,
        "name": "kitmehsu",
        "username": "kitmehsu",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/kitmehsu/{size}/1901_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-07-23T21:36:58.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Now, I've read that the order of operations is incorrect in the rule book, and that you score prisms before resolving &nbsp;crashes, but that resulted ina question in today's game. A player using cosmonauts power tried to jump through a laser piece using his ability and didn't fully pass through the line (only the point was on the other laser) with a prism on the other side. Since he didn't crash the turn he used his power yet didn't pass the laser fully, we ruled he'd crash next turn. The problem was, there was debate on weather he'd be aloud to score the prism since his point of crashing was before he'd reach the prism.</p><p>So here's the short of it: &nbsp;can you crash into a laser to score a prism on the other side of it?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:49:46.706Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 10,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 50.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 16890,
        "topic_slug": "crashing-and-scoring",
        "display_username": "kitmehsu",
        "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
        "flair_bg_color": "",
        "flair_color": "",
        "flair_group_id": 41,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
        "can_delete": false,
